The function will determine the quarter of the year based on the month number. The mapping is as follows: January to March (1-3) is Quarter 1, April to June (4-6) is Quarter 2, July to September (7-9) is Quarter 3, and October to December (10-12) is Quarter 4. I am confident in this solution.

```python
def quarter(month):
    if 1 <= month <= 3:
        return 1
    elif 4 <= month <= 6:
        return 2
    elif 7 <= month <= 9:
        return 3
    elif 10 <= month <= 12:
        return 4
    else:
        return None  # Invalid month
```
